infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Unbounded vs bounded fan-out: the one decision
  desc Promise.all(map) starts all N at once; a limiter caps in-flight at k — same disease, opposite outcome
  compares
    - label Unbounded Promise.all(map)
      children
        - label All N in flight at once
          desc A million ids becomes a million pending promises instantly
        - label Memory piles up, OOM-killed
          desc Buffers, closures, pending promises accumulate
        - label Downstream gets hammered
          desc Opens connections until the database refuses
        - label Fast start, then collapse
          desc Past what downstream absorbs: only queueing and failures
        - label Latent outage if N is uncontrolled
          desc Attacker- or data-sized array is a self-inflicted DoS
    - label Bounded limiter (limit k)
      children
        - label At most k in flight
          desc p-limit(20) or worker pool pulls as capacity frees
        - label Memory stays predictable
          desc Live set bounded regardless of total item count
        - label Respects downstream limits
          desc Connection pool, API rate limit, disk IOPS
        - label Fast and stable
          desc Unbounded does not beat bounded
        - label k = downstream capacity
          desc Largest k it tolerates, not infinity (e.g. pool of 20)
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
